## Canonical Minimal PHP Scaffolds
- `ext.php`:
```php
<?php
/**
 * RAVEN CMS
 * ~/private/ext/{slug}/ext.php
 * Extension service bootstrap provider.
 * docs: /private/ext/AGENTS.md
 */
declare(strict_types=1);

return [
    'storage' => [
        // Supported options:
        // 'local' => true,
        // 'table' => true,
        // 'tables' => ['items'],
        // 'aux' => ['finger'],
        // 'panel' => true,
        // 'public' => true,  // module only
        // 'bin' => true,     // symlinks private/bin/ -> private/ext/{slug}/bin/
    ],
    // Set to true to declare that this extension provides cron.php.
    // Core registers extension as a scheduler source; rvn-cron loads cron.php at run time.
    // 'scheduler' => true,
    'boot' => static function (array &$rvn): void {
        // Use $rvn['extension_storage']['{slug}'] for resolved storage roots.
        // Register extension services into $rvn['extension_services'] when needed.
        // Values may be concrete service objects or lazy zero-arg closures that
        // Raven resolves through extension_services_for('{slug}') on first use.
        // To register a shortcode runtime: $rvn['extension_services']['{slug}']['shortcode_runtimes'][] = $runtime;
    },
];
```
